          %h3#StabilizationHypothesis Stabilization hypothesis
          %p
            A proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization+hypothesis"} stabilization hypothesis
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-categories
            is a byproduct of corollary 1.1.10 of (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie
            ), stated as example 1.2.3.
          %h3#AdditivityTheorem Additivity theorem
          %p
            It has been long conjectured that it should be true that when suitably defined, there is a tensor product of
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mi k
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ′
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mi k
                      %mo ′
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{E}_k \otimes \mathbb{E}_{k'} \simeq \mathbb{E}_{k + k'}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is discussed and realized in section 1.2. of (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie
            ). The tensor product is defined in appendix B.7.
          %h3#RelationToFultonMacPhersonOperad Relation to Fulton-MacPherson operad
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+operad"} Fulton-MacPherson operad
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weakly equivalent
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} model structure on operads
              with respect to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+n-disk+operad"} little n-disk operad
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Salvatore01"}> Salvatore 01, Prop. 4.9
            , summarized as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volic 14, Prop. 5.6
          %h3#cohomology_formality Cohomology: Formality
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+little+n-disk+operad+is+formal"} the little n-disk operad is formal
          %h3#homology_poisson_operads Homology: Poisson operads
          %p
            For an
            = succeed "-operad" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_k
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            is the
            %span.newWikiWord
              Poisson operad
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Poisson+operad"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{k}
          %p
            See for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Costello"}> Costello
            ) and see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+n-algebra"} Poisson n-algebra
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Explicit models of
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barratt-Eccles+operad"} Barratt-Eccles operad
          %p (…)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"}> configuration space of points
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+operad"} Fulton-MacPherson operad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebra"} factorization algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+operad"} A-∞ operad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+operad"} E-∞ operad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+operad"} L-∞ operad
          %h2#references References
          %p A comprehensive reference for many known models is
          %ul
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord>
                André Beuckelmann
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Andr%C3%A9+Beuckelmann"} ?
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  A small catalogue of
                  = succeed "-operads" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03842v1"} arXiv:2212.03842v1
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li#Fresse18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benoit+Fresse"}> Benoit Fresse
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Little discs operads, graph complexes and Grothendieck–Teichmüller groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haynes+Miller"} Haynes Miller
              (ed.)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Homotopy+Theory"} Handbook of Homotopy Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.12536"}> arXiv:1811.12536
              )
          %p A standard textbook reference is chapter 4 of
          %ul
            %li#May
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              ,
              %em The geometry of iterated loop spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/geom_iter.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The equivalence to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+operad"} Fulton-MacPherson operad
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Salvatore01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Salvatore"}> Paolo Salvatore
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Configuration spaces with summable labels
          %p
            Proof that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+little+n-disk+operad+is+formal"} the little n-disk operad is formal
            was sketched by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"} Maxim Kontsevich
            and spelled out in
          %ul
            %li#LambrechtsVolic14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pascal+Lambrechts"}> Pascal Lambrechts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismar+Voli%C4%87"} Ismar Volić
              = succeed "," do
                %em Formality of the little N-disks operad
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/memo/1079"} doi:10.1090/memo/1079
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
            ‘ work on
            = succeed "-actions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"} John Francis
              PhD thesis (
              %a{:href => "http://dspace.mit.edu/handle/1721.1/43792"}> web
              )
          %p This influenced the revised version of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Commutative+Algebra"} Commutative Algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0703204"}> arXiv
              )
          %p and is extended to include a discussion of traces and centers in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"} John Francis
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
                %em Integral transforms and Drinfeld Centers in Derived Geometry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0805.0157"}> arXiv
                )
              %p
                (see also
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-function+theory"} geometric ∞-function theory
          %p
            A detailed discussion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_k
            in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-operads"} (∞,1)-operads
            is in
          %ul#Lurie
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}[k]
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ek-Algebras"} Algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/DAG-VI.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            An elementary computation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            of the little
            = succeed "-disk" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em solar system calculus
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dev+Sinha"}> Dev Sinha
              ,
              %em The homology of the little disks operad
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0610236"}> arXiv:math/0610236
              )
          %p For the relation to Poisson Operads see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
              %em
                Factorization algebras in perturbative quantum field theory :
                = succeed "-operad" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi P
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_0
